            <ArticleTitle>Acute scrotum: an exceptional presentation of acute nonperforated appendicitis in childhood.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1435-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Acute scrotum is an exceptional form of presentation of acute appendicitis in the pediatric age group. Only 14 cases have been described in literature. The authors report a case of an 8-year-old boy with a 12-hour history of right hemiscrotal pain secondary to acute retrocecal nonperforated appendicitis. Surgical exploration showed a patent &quot;processus vaginalis.&quot;</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
